        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9f09cdaa58644cc69bf2000165e87aee",
      "statement": "The architectural keyboard FIFO is 16 entries deep, polled through KBD_STATUS at 0xF0060 and KBD_DATA at 0xF0062.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://rtl/deep16_top.sv#L148-L158",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bb34e1d165586b0e85bf0e8b6af489be984253b034743421b45f9526db5f250b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_faac322ccd004eabaef582ceb8d809f1",
      "statement": "ps2_rx decodes Set-2 frames as start bit, eight data bits LSB first, odd parity and stop, drops bad frames with a sticky frame_error, and looks ASCII up in a 2048x8 BSRAM table addressed by ctrl, caps, shift and scan code; extended 0xE0 keys are ignored.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://rtl/ps2_rx.sv#L1-L16",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3f7c208138c7ff957789d4538b8dd979cb746cb89e33127e75974bb94804bf3e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_96ae896cea0b4a94b636b88a3bcaed53",
      "statement": "The board pushes each decoded PS/2 ASCII byte into both the architectural keyboard FIFO and the UART receive FIFO, and each build's software reads only one of them.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://rtl/deep16_board.sv#L415-L425",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:40b94a480f9fe308b5a44d02418fb00800312272a9e56cc3e39aab78df44f786:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cebb933dda5e4ab394c33e9e0187a9ea",
      "statement": "The timer at 0xF0020 is a 32-bit millisecond counter with a 32-bit compare, a sticky match flag and an IRQ enable bit, and its compare resets to 0xFFFFFFFF so a fresh machine never matches.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://rtl/deep16_timer.sv#L1-L20",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4d0c6f01d42e95db7301ae789080dfb6123188140731e4158ee0147c5ed26a94:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://rtl/deep16_timer.sv#L40-L50",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bf4a5b403fbd25c474d31c9c12feaf26d3a81990a7ea0c893e89752b9ad28e80:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d6096f9141654ed988a27ea743d111a7",
      "statement": "At 6.75 MHz the timer's millisecond prescaler is 6750 cycles and a separate divider produces the 15 kHz tick that drives SIC source bit 1.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://rtl/deep16_timer.sv#L55-L75",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ff99520e3d5c01d1e460e92299c62a74cdfbe573b57d067fda15d753ba06cb41:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_908f1a1f7e0f404aa1b4c9926ef4d016",
      "statement": "The D16nano build exposes a read-only 32-bit CPU cycle counter at 0xF0068/0xF006A and a display-status word at 0xF0066 with vertical blank, frame toggle, S2, UART RX-ready and the synchronised raster toggle as bits 0-4.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://rtl/deep16_board.sv#L333-L345",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fc9c8cff6ad47d7f25aadca4028a00388038d6b96c9b70ddb5184c5bf1d24678:"
        },
        {
